  "$comment": "Single source of truth for the Luxar gallery harness. Consumed by BOTH scripts/gallery/generate_gallery_datasets.py (dataset generation) and packages/luxar-viewer/src/tests/screenshots/generate-gallery.spec.ts (still + orbit-video capture). Add a demo here to include it in the gallery; nothing else needs updating. The authoritative field list is the DemoEntry interface in generate-gallery.spec.ts; this comment and scripts/gallery/README.md must be kept in step with it. REQUIRED: id (gallery media filename stem + dataset stem), title (caption), geometry, category, script (demo_*.py under packages/luxar/src/luxar/demos, or null if the demo lives only on a feature branch and its dataset must be pre-generated), dataset (path under datasets/demos, relative to repo root). OPTIONAL: exposure (log2-stops override; omit for auto-exposure), autoFrame (default true; set false for very heavy scenes to skip fill-to-screen and use the baked camera), autoExpose (default true; set false to use the demo's baked exposure), fillTarget (per-demo screen-coverage target for fill-to-screen; default 0.95), zoom (multiplicative zoom after fill: >1 in, <1 out), distance (absolute camera distance in world units — bypasses fill; for faint/diffuse subjects), viewAngle ({azimuth, elevation} in degrees — orients the camera before framing), orbitUp ('x'|'y'|'z' world up-axis the rock revolves about; default y; use z for a subject lying along Z), dimensionNav ({key, steps} for nD demos), timelapse ({framePoint} — advance the time dim while recording a 4D series; framePoint = fraction of the range used to frame the still), lodFinest (default true; set false for a very heavy scene so the coverage-based LOD may pick a lighter level), readme (true = a current top pick for the README gallery), note (free-text human annotation; the capture code never reads it).",
