      "fillTarget": 0.84,
      "note": "the first SHADED tile. A headlit surface has N.L~1 on every visible facet, so its lit histogram is only 0.06 wide (p10 0.840, p50 0.873, p99 0.903); driving that p99 to the 0.9 target parks the WHOLE subject in the ACES highlight rolloff, which desaturates toward white - membrane saturation measured 0.28 against 0.85 authored. The clip guard cannot catch it either, being a tail test on a distribution with no tail. That is now the auto-exposure flat-subject pass's job: spread 0.063 is well under NARROW_SPREAD_MAX, so it re-targets the median and comes down ~1.5 stops on its own. These are the numbers exposure-policy.ts was calibrated on, so this tile deliberately carries NO exposure override - it is the case that pass exists for. Framing still needs one: the default 0.95 fill clips the slab off the bottom and both sides, and 0.84 fits it whole at 82pct coverage"
    },
